Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 22:54:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): dashboard comments record an agent courier's
 writer_kind; human is never client-assertable [daveey]

The Desktop session-mentions courier serves the agent cross_task tool by POSTing to
/api/plugins/kanban/tasks/<id>/comments, the endpoint the Kanban drawer uses. It hardcoded
writer_kind='human', so an agent's cross-gateway comment (comment 179201 on t_01a1c753e58ef690)
reached the running worker as "from the operator". The agent-261aa31f49 fix (1915, c2f066a6d0)
only covered the in-process kanban_comment tool and assumed every dashboard writer is a person.

The endpoint now takes writer_kind='agent' (+ writer_session) from the courier. A client may only
lower provenance: human stays the endpoint's own default for GUI comments, and an explicit
'human', an unknown kind, or a session without a kind is a 400 with nothing stored. The actor
resolution lives in plugin_api_comment_actor.py (facade size cap).

Tests: tests/tools/test_kanban_dashboard_comment_actor.py (agent+session, agent without session,
GUI authors desktop/user/dashboard/none stay human, 5 forged/malformed refusals store nothing,
live note to a running worker says "another agent session" for the courier and "the operator"
for the GUI). Card t_01a1c78af452ff15.
